// The derived validator tag, end to end: EVSEStatusEnumType strips to
// EVSEStatusType (the enum naming rule), lower-cases only its first word
// ("EVSE", the whole initialism run, not just "E") to get evseStatusType,
// and appends the literal "201" — evseStatusType201. This is where the
// tag is actually observable: RenderDefinition itself never emits a
// registration call, only a referencing property's validate tag carries it.

EVSEStatus EVSEStatusType `json:"evseStatus,omitempty" validate:"omitempty,evseStatusType201"`
